{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game","id":1039592,"title":"Looking for a PbP Mage game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-28T14:04:58-08:00","id":1039592,"title":"Looking for a PbP Mage game","content":"I am looking to join a Mage: the Awakening 2e PbP game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T06:47:57-08:00","id":1043520,"title":"","content":"Me likewise.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T23:04:44-08:00","id":1043867,"title":"","content":"Yep, me three. Boy howdy it sure would be nice if someone ran one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder","name":"Silver_Smoulder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12852_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T08:16:54-08:00","id":1043989,"title":"","content":"I've considered it before, but I don't know 2e at all. Only 1e. I've run lots of CoD 1e games before in real life, but I feel like I'd only flub 2e until I play in one myself. Plus I've never played PbP. I'll read up I guess and post again if I feel like I get it. Until then we'll just hae to wait for an ST (i'd love to play mummy 2e too).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12808-dissapatideum","name":"DissapatiDeum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T09:23:20-08:00","id":1044018,"title":"","content":"Well I now that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a> is getting ready to run a game and I am hoping a PbP game that I can join. He has a thread that says players stay out and so I haven't looked at it just in case he runs it here or somewhere else that I could join.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T09:54:53-08:00","id":1044039,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that thread is for a game Axelgear is running in person.<br /> <br /> Not a commitment from me, just a suggestion: would y'all want to play a Mage game in the To The Strongest setting from Dark Eras? If I ran something, it would be an episodic traveling game where each Chapter centers on a particular weird thing/mystery/monster in the ancient world. This would definitely be a low-stress game that doesn't require a ton of long posts from me or you. If I ran it, I would minimize the amount of background reading you need to do, and present the historical setting in a very player-facing way that emphasizes the stuff that's relevant to you. More like adventuring in an exotic fantasy setting than reading a history lecture.<br /> <br /> Any interest in that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T10:00:15-08:00","id":1044043,"title":"","content":"I actually have a character made specifically for that Era <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T10:26:37-08:00","id":1044059,"title":"","content":"Oh, nice! What's their deal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T10:50:26-08:00","id":1044075,"title":"","content":"The base concept was to be someone to balance Death and Matter, then have as many story hooks with CoD Kemet as possible (I'm talking Influence (Cult of Phoenix), Contacts (Khaibit) level of hooks). Familiar and Sleeper life ate up all of his Merits, though.<br /> <br /> Now he's just a junior scribe who became a Scribe (that is, Jnanashakti) and is being bamboozled by his Familiar into thinking she's an emissary of Anubis (she's just a wolf spirit) to goad him into Resonant behavior (fun fact: she agrees with the Libertine stereotype on Mystagogues, he'll probably take grave robbing as cultural Hybris, no way that'd go wrong /s).<br /> <br /> Edit: do you allow specialities and/or Professional Training to apply to Rote mudras?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":6508,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","user":"Tambov","date":". 02-05-2017, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T10:51:05-08:00","id":1044076,"title":"","content":"I'm afraid I'll have to disappoint; I assembled the group a while ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T11:12:06-08:00","id":1044085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1044039#post1044039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that thread is for a game Axelgear is running in person.<br /> <br /> Not a commitment from me, just a suggestion: would y'all want to play a Mage game in the To The Strongest setting from Dark Eras? If I ran something, it would be an episodic traveling game where each Chapter centers on a particular weird thing/mystery/monster in the ancient world. This would definitely be a low-stress game that doesn't require a ton of long posts from me or you. If I ran it, I would minimize the amount of background reading you need to do, and present the historical setting in a very player-facing way that emphasizes the stuff that's relevant to you. More like adventuring in an exotic fantasy setting than reading a history lecture.<br /> <br /> Any interest in that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would be willing I have no Idea what the o The Strongest setting from Dark Eras is but if you let me know what book I would need I can buy that book. I do not have the Dark Era books but was planing on buying them anyway. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1044076#post1044076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm afraid I'll have to disappoint; I assembled the group a while ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bummer if you need a replacement or decide to add another seat please keep me in mind. I would love to play in a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T11:41:22-08:00","id":1044103,"title":"","content":"Basically Mages from different corners of Alexander the Macedonian's empire meet up in each other's lands, investigate local mysteries and notice similarities between Greek, Egyptian, Persian and Indian Awakened traditions. In particular they notice similar schools of thought that will later become the Diamond Orders.<br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/178583/Chronicles-of-Darkness-Dark-Eras\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/...ness-Dark-Eras</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T11:45:49-08:00","id":1044104,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6508_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6508\" data-vbnamecard=\"6508\">Tambov</a> That seems cool, I like the familiar especially. I'd love to use the sha from Sothis Ascends or something like them in this setting, so that's something to keep in mind. I'm down with crossover but be aware that (if I run it) this would be a location-hopping game where knowing the Khaibit is more useful in some areas than others, and you're not gonna be in Kemet all the time. The region that I know the most about in this period is India, FYI. Then again, the whole point of the Era is cultural exchange and cross-contamination across regions.<br /> <br /> Professional Training and Specialties only apply to mundane skills in my games. That's what rote specialties are for, ya goof! I've been running Mage 2E for a while and I think I have a good idea now of how exactly spellcasting is designed to interact with dice math; it works best when bonuses only come from very specifically defined sources.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> So in the book Dark Eras, one of the settings is called To The Strongest. It's set right after Alexander the Great dies in 323 BCE. The main hook for the setting is that the Orders and some other ideas from the modern setting haven't formed yet, and mages from these different traditions in Greece, Egypt, Persia and India are only just now meeting and exchanging ideas about magic. Culture clash, worlds collide, fighting monsters and uncovering lost wisdom in the ancient world, that kinda stuff. If I ran it, I'd be keeping 90% of the historical stuff on my side of the DM screen and providing you guys with what you need to know as more of an adventure fantasy D&amp;D type thing. If you wanted to get a book, get Dark Eras, but I'd wait until we know whether the game is happening and a good fit before you buy anything. Again, I'd just tell you guys the stuff you need to know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T13:25:23-08:00","id":1044152,"title":"","content":"I have budgeted $100.00 every 2 weeks to books and I haven't spent that yet the period so I was looking at what I wanted to buy and that was at the top of the list<br /> <br /> So there is no orders yet and the paths are the same correct?<br /> <br /> A concept off the top of my head would be a wandering Egyptian (Obrimos or Acanthus) mage tracking a terrible beast that ransacked a small village just outside of Cairo.<br /> <br /> When I get/read the book I will probably have a better idea of what I want to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T14:22:15-08:00","id":1044179,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> That sounds really cool.Will definitely have to look into the Dark Eras book then.<br /> <br /> And count me in if you decide to run the game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12884-arudin","name":"Arudin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T14:39:49-08:00","id":1044190,"title":"","content":"Just noticed this thread. I am always up for a Mage game.<br /> <br /> Some ideas off the top of my head:<br /> Devout Obrimos Zoroastrian Magi who noticed that the occult readings of the stars are different in various locations and believe it is a message from Ahura Mazda. Traveling around to take astrological readings.<br /> <br /> Ex Mummy cultist Acanthus acting as an agent of fate, going around making small changes that will ripple in big ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T22:06:04-08:00","id":1044377,"title":"","content":"I've got a 1E pbp game that could always use players. PM me for details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T22:28:05-08:00","id":1044386,"title":"","content":"That sounds pretty fun.<br /> <br /> As for me, I want to play an Obrimos Magewright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder","name":"Silver_Smoulder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12852_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T01:42:34-08:00","id":1044421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grey_goose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1044377#post1044377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a 1E pbp game that could always use players. PM me for details.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unfortunately I do not know that system and from what I can see looking at the differences from 1e to 2e it is alot to learn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T15:02:16-08:00","id":1044739,"title":"","content":"Okay, looks like there's some interest. I'll put a post together about the setting, and we can start talking about character ideas and a structure for the game.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1144_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1144\" data-vbnamecard=\"1144\">Exthalion</a> Both of those are good and appealing. Feel free to come up with other ideas too, but I'd be into either of those. A wandering Persian stargazer sounds cool.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12852_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12852\" data-vbnamecard=\"12852\">Silver_Smoulder</a> What do you mean by Magewright? Like a magic item crafter?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> Tracking a beast is a good hook that I can do a lot with. Once I post about the setting, we can flesh it out a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T16:27:31-08:00","id":1044766,"title":"","content":"Then I will put more thought into the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T17:42:45-08:00","id":1044786,"title":"","content":"<u><b>To the Strongest</b></u><br /> <br /> I'm not going to be super worried about historical accuracy from you guys (or me), I just want to paint a basic picture of what's happening in the world and where the important places are.<br /> <br /> The setting picks up in 323 BCE. You live in the <b>Alexandrian Empire</b>, a completely new construct made up of the many kingdoms his armies have conquered: Greece, Persia, Egypt, up to the edge of India. Over the last 15 years or so, Alexander has started from northern Greece and conquered almost the entire known world. Many, many people refer to him as a god. Along with war and destruction, this has been an opportunity for cultural exchange and sharing ideas, as various ancient rival cultures are now united under one ruler. Main idea: your world is currently experiencing massive, catastrophic change and upheaval, and no one really knows what the future holds. All bets are off.<br /> <br /> <b>Greece</b> has traditionally been divided among rival city-states with a shared culture and language, but Alexander has united them into one part of the empire. Most of his soldiers are Greek, and Greeks are the ones doing the majority of the traveling to other cultures. Thermopylae, Socrates, Plato, all that famous stuff happened within the last century. Greece (or Hellas, as in &quot;Alexander is spreading Hellenic culture&quot;) is now entering a new era where Athens and Sparta are just two more cities in a massive empire. The empire has historically been dominated by Greek culture, but it's absorbing and spreading other cultures as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Persia</b> was an empire covering most of the modern Middle East, and the regional superpower, until Alexander's armies conquered it 8 years ago at the Battle of Gaugamela. These are the main guys Alexander had been fighting. The major religion is Zoroastrianism, which is all about sacred fire and written scriptures and angels/devils and dualistic Good vs Evil, but the Persian (Achaemenid) empire also contained the former Babylonia and Judah/Israel and lots of other cultures that are now in the broader mix. Alexander is super fascinated by Persian culture, he married a local woman, and his Greek generals and soldiers are very unhappy about it. In 323, Alexander is hanging out in the city of Babylon planning his next move.<br /> <br /> <b>Egypt</b> (the locals call it Kemet) is very ancient and magical. Everyone knows they had a hugely powerful society for thousands of years. 99% of the population lives in cities and towns along the Nile, covered with ancient monuments and temples and tombs, and also busy modern trading ports. The Egyptians have been a subject people for a few centuries now, most recently to the Persians, but the culture and wisdom of their ancestors is highly respected. Alexander established the (culturally Greek) city of Alexandria here about 8 years ago, future site of the Library of Alexandria, after taking Egypt from Persia. There are also lots of famous and, again, very ancient cities like Memphis, Elephantine, Swenet, Bubastis, Abydos...(Cairo doesn't exist yet but Memphis is close.)<br /> <br /> <b>India</b> is the edge of the known world. There is no single ruler of India (at this exact moment), but the various medium-sized kingdoms and smaller territories have many shared cultural and religious assumptions based on sacrifice, renunciation, and reincarnation. 3 years ago, Alexander won a costly victory against an Indian king (war elephants and all) at the Battle of the Hydaspes, and his homesick army subsequently &quot;persuaded&quot; him to turn back once he reached the base of the Himalayas. The army retreated to Babylon, but there's a vibrant Greek-Indian cultural exchange happening along the towns (Nicaea and Bucephala) and trade routes they established up to the monsoon-swollen Hydaspes river.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Still with me? Alright. Let's talk about the Mage-specific stuff.<br /> <br /> The whole mass-conquest thing is a rare opportunity for Awakened from very different cultures to meet each other and realize that they're using different words to describe the same things. Each of those 4 regions I described has its own overarching magical traditions called a Great Cult, but as mages travel the Empire, they start to form Darshanas, semi-formal societies and philosophical schools based on deeper ideas about the purpose of magic, rather than their cultural background. Instead of Orders, mages in this setting have a Great Cult and a Darshana that together provide the same benefits. Your Darshana is kinda primary, and your approach to that Darshana is informed by your Great Cult. Read the Dark Eras chapter, it has lots of helpful examples.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Darshanas</b></u><br /> <br /> The <b>Jnanashakti</b> or <b>Gnostikon</b> are scholars and teachers who study the world in search of magic. Similar to the Mysterium.<br /> <br /> The <b>Mahanizrayani</b> or <b>Omphalos</b> are priests and leaders who guide Sleepers, travel between the magical worlds, and keep those worlds and their creatures separate for the good of humanity. Similar to the Silver Ladder.<br /> <br /> The <b>Samashti</b> or <b>Phulakeion</b> are mystics and deceivers who hunt dark magic and perform immoral acts for the greater good, damning themselves so the world can Ascend. Similar to the Guardians of the Veil.<br /> <br /> The <b>Vajrastra</b> or <b>Adamantine Arrow</b> are warriors and soldiers who do Adamantine Arrow stuff. Existence is war, find purpose through combat, prove yourself worthy of the gift of magic by emulating heroes, etc. Very popular Darshana in a world convulsed by war and roaming armies.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Great Cults</b></u><br /> <br /> The <b>Arcadian Mysteries</b> (or <i>Pelasgians</i>) are Greek, philosophers with big ideas about the Realm of Forms and reshaping the world like Alexander has. [cultural lens: Greek gods and titans.]<br /> <br /> The <b>Karpani</b> (or <i>Magi</i>) are Persian, rural poets and singers who've had to step into a bigger role since the Zoroastrian high mage-priests were scattered. [Zoroastrian angels and demons.]<br /> <br /> The <b>Weret-Hekau</b> (or <i>Hemka</i>) are Egyptian, heirs to a truly ancient tradition who manipulate the soul and try to protect their inherited glories from outsiders. [Egyptian gods and five-part soul.]<br /> <br /> The <b>Mantra Sadikhi</b> (or <i>Mantrikis</i>) are Indian, wandering ascetics and nomads who try to see the world clearly and act without delusion. [Hindu and Buddhist gods and lore.]<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> That's the big stuff. There are also some more fiddly terminology and setting changes that you can read the chapter for if you want, they aren't as relevant for character creation. Dark Eras page 79 has a helpful quick reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T18:05:53-08:00","id":1044792,"title":"","content":"Feel free to start thinking and talking about characters, but don't worry about stats or character sheets yet. FYI though, you wouldn't be newly Awakened or anything, you'd be somewhat experienced with some XP under your belt.<br /> <br /> Here's the game I would want to run: all of you have a shared Mentor, a powerful but distant mage who spends most of her time these days politicking at Alexander's court. You can be as close or casual with this NPC as you want, and we'll design them together, they're basically just an excuse to provide campaign structure and keep the party together. You have agreed to form a cabal and look into various things on your Mentor's behalf throughout the Empire, in exchange for patronage and opportunities to learn and develop your magic.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking each Chapter would be based in a different town/city/area, and you would always have an overarching Thing To Do, but you could do other stuff if it interested you more. Like an episodic game.<br /> <br /> Does that sound fun, or does anyone have a different idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T19:08:21-08:00","id":1044819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1044792#post1044792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feel free to start thinking and talking about characters, but don't worry about stats or character sheets yet. FYI though, you wouldn't be newly Awakened or anything, you'd be somewhat experienced with some XP under your belt.<br /> <br /> Here's the game I would want to run: all of you have a shared Mentor, a powerful but distant mage who spends most of her time these days politicking at Alexander's court. You can be as close or casual with this NPC as you want, and we'll design them together, they're basically just an excuse to provide campaign structure and keep the party together. You have agreed to form a cabal and look into various things on your Mentor's behalf throughout the Empire, in exchange for patronage and opportunities to learn and develop your magic.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking each Chapter would be based in a different town/city/area, and you would always have an overarching Thing To Do, but you could do other stuff if it interested you more. Like an episodic game.<br /> <br /> Does that sound fun, or does anyone have a different idea?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That all sounds good and I purchaced the book last night so I will start reading it in depth, I started last night by skinning the To the Strongest. Here is the start of the character, I will fluff it out as I read more and get a feel for the mentor and the other players. Some of the below is just notes as I build the character.<br /> <br /> Setau \u2013 Warrior Priest<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Name:</b> Hm nTr Anpu (Servant of Anubis)<br /> <br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros<br /> <b>Darshanas:</b> Vajrastra<br /> <b>Great Cult:</b> Weret-Hekau<br /> <b>Legacy:</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Stone Scribes</a><br /> <br /> Follower of Anpu (Anubis).<br /> <br /> The Five Part Souls (notes)<br /> <b>Ren:</b> Fate (the name)<br /> <b>Ba:</b> Mind (Identity and passion)<br /> <b>Sheut:</b> Death (Shadow Aspects)<br /> <b>Ka:</b> Prime (vital essence)<br /> <b>Ab:</b> Spirit (Heart of the Soul)<br /> <br /> Setau was an architect by trade prior to the Awakening, viewed that Awakening as a sign from the God and became a Warrior Priest. Father was an Official in Memphis.<br /> <br /> Left Egypt to track a great beast (a Baalim) that decimated a small village outside of Memphis. Tracking the Beast to Babylon where he lost track of it. Near to Alexanders Court he sought assistance in tracking the beast in unfamiliar territory. This would introduce him to his mentor and a group of other wandering mages. He befriended his soon to be mentor as he pledged his service.<br /> <br /> On one knee \u201cBy the Might of the all-powerful Anubis, I pledge my service\u201d and thus his journey began.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 02-07-2017, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T08:36:01-08:00","id":1045087,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> Yes, a magic item crafter. I think this will be especially interesting in this early-world setting, because all the stories of items of power have to come from somewhere, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (The implication is that my guy will be the one responsible for crafting stuff like the Aegis, Hades' Invisibility Helmet.) Oooh, I can even have one eye, have my Shadowname be &quot;Cyclops&quot; or &quot;Hephaestus,&quot; depending on how I want to do this.<br /> <br /> Also, I just want to clarify - I thought the Diamond Orders existed since the Fall. I don't have issue with these Cults, but which is the true history?<br /> <br /> Also, the Sleeping Curse? I understand that we're still subject to the Abyss and Paradox, but to Sleepers still unravel spells, since they are more likely to believe in magic and accept it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12852,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder","user":"Silver_Smoulder","date":". 02-07-2017, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder","name":"Silver_Smoulder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12852_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T09:20:26-08:00","id":1045136,"title":"","content":"BTW, how many players are you looking for. There were 6 people that posted interest in this thread. Also are we using this thread as more or less the recruitment thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T10:30:59-08:00","id":1045209,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> Perfect, I like it, very cool! There's a Moros PC in my IRL game that's really into Anubis, so I've got some ideas for you. I might leave open exactly what the monster is, and we'll figure out exactly where you guys start geographically once more characters come in.<br /> <br /> This is basically the recruit thread, yeah. If anyone is reading this thread and wants to apply, go for it. I don't want to have an extended process where I turn a ton of people away though. I'll cap it at like 4-5 players, it depends on how many people actually post characters. I'm spoiled by my IRL game where I only have 3 PCs, I really want to keep the game from getting too big and time-consuming to update on my end.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12852_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12852\" data-vbnamecard=\"12852\">Silver_Smoulder</a> The fake-out about the Diamond Orders is one of the fun parts about this setting! As a big ol' history nerd, I really like it- it turns out, just like most people, mages in the 21st century believe a lot of stuff about the past that isn't quite accurate. I encourage you to check out the book, because the chapter deeply addresses all of those questions in a cool way, but I'll summarize it here.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">There were some setting changes from 1E to 2E, and in 2E the standard belief among mages in 2017 is that Atlantis is more of a mythical place than a literal city that was physically destroyed in the year 1537 BC or something. They know for sure that there was once an openly magical culture that fell and was removed from time and space, and there are Artifacts and ruins around the world that seemingly were left behind by that culture (or several cultures), but the specifics are harder to figure out. Atlantis is a common metaphor for understanding that lost culture, and actually the whole Atlantis and Diamond Orders philosophy is <i>just now starting to develop </i>during To The Strongest as Greek philosopher-mages encounter other magical traditions and share ideas. I'll quote the 2E core book on how the modern Orders see themselves:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the ideal Awakened society postulated by the Diamond\u2019s<br /> Atlantean symbolism, the Adamantine Arrow embodies <i>Ungula<br /> Draconis</i>, the Talon of the Dragon: righteous warriors who fight to<br /> keep the flame of human power alive in an age of darkness.<br /> [..]<br /> In Atlantean symbolism, the Guardians embody the all-seeing<br /> oculus, <i>Visus Draconis</i>. The Eye of the Dragon scrutinizes every<br /> detail of the Awakened City with an unflinching gaze.<br /> [...]<br /> In Diamond symbolism, the Mysterium are the <i>Alae Draconis</i>:<br /> the Wings of the Dragon, uplifting the Awakened City\u2019s body<br /> politic with winds of insight.<br /> [...]<br /> The Ladder is responsible for the Diamond\u2019s claim to wisdom<br /> from an ancient ur-culture, and it strives ever to maintain that<br /> magical symbolism in the form of the Diamond and Pentacle.<br /> They are <i>Vox Draconis</i>: Voice of the Dragon, priests of Atlantis,<br /> granted primacy not because of conferred authority or divine<br /> right but recognition of wise leadership. </div> </div> </div>That Atlantean symbolism doesn't fully exist yet during To The Strongest. Mages from different cultures don't see themselves as all being one thing with a single shared heritage, they instead view their magic through Sleeper mythic ideas: the Great Cults. However, it's the Darshanas that will later develop into the Diamond Orders, shared philosophies of magic that are starting to transcend one specific culture and mythology. A Victorian Time mage who was spying on the past might hypothesize that the Darshanas are mages beginning to rediscover their shared past in Atlantis that was scattered by the Fall, but an Alexandrian mage doesn't see it that way in the present. However, most of the Great Cults <i>do </i>believe in Ages of Man, where humans in a previous era of heroes and gods and monsters were wiser, stronger, and worked magic openly. But over time, humanity degraded in subsequent ages, and in the present age magic is hidden and humans are in darkness.<br /> <br /> As for the Sleeping Curse: again, Dark Eras talks about this in depth, but I'll summarize. Rules-wise, everything is the same, Sleepers still unravel magic and cause Paradox. It's not about belief in magic, but failure to understand. If your character told a random Sleeper that they were a magician, they would probably be skeptical, but they might well believe you (and perhaps warn their friends to be careful around you, or inform the authorities.) That belief wouldn't stop them from unraveling your magic if you cast a spell in front of them. It's not about a modern idea of &quot;different realities clashing&quot;, it's just that you're Wise and they aren't. You perceive the world more truly than they do, so of course they can't perceive your pure magic. It's all the same single world, there aren't multiple dimensions or anything, but you see it more clearly than most people. You're probably not going to see a vampire ruling openly as an undead king or something, but rural people especially might warn you to avoid the river crossing because a monster lives there. The supernatural is hidden, but many people know/believe that it's out there somewhere, and some claim (truly or falsely, there are still plenty of charlatans) to have contact with it.<br /> <br /> Mages in the Alexandrian era don't believe in Paradox (same mechanics though) or a single Abyss that's eating reality with every spell. Instead, poorly-controlled spells cause <b>Nemesis</b>, which is caused by lack of virtue and self-control, as well as demons from the primordial Chaos that every Cult sees differently. If you're a Greek/Hellenic mage, you identify that chaos with Erebus, the formless primordial darkness where the Titans are imprisoned. This is easily proven, because a mage can summon those lesser Titans (that modern mages call Gulmoth) from the darkness. It's an extremely dangerous practice that only the foolish or extremely brave would attempt (much like conquering the world, as Alexander has), but it's not viewed as an abhorrent &quot;crime against reality&quot; or anything. As a matter of fact, the shattered Babylonian Great Cult called the <i>Baalim </i>were known and feared for their mastery of Chaos and summoning devils from it. Modern mages would call them <i>Scelesti</i>, but that term doesn't exist yet. No Latin!<br /> <br /> And just a few words about early-world and stories about items of power! One-eyed or otherwise wounded craftsman is a solid concept and you should run with it, but just to be clear, people in the Alexandrian era don't see themselves as being in the &quot;early world.&quot; Egyptian culture has existed for thousands of years, Mesopotamian empires have come and gone, and it's widely believed by educated people that the age of heroes and myths has passed. Just as an example, most Greeks see Egypt as a place of faded ancient wisdom and magic, and the Weret-Hekau specialize in long-lost items of power (if they can just find the damn things.) Sleepers know the stories about the Golden Fleece and the helmet of Hades and stuff, and they wouldn't expect someone to make something like that in their lifetime. But those are the kinds of legends and figures that the Great Cults draw on for their view of magic. You could absolutely play a Greek crafter who explicitly says &quot;I create magical items worthy of the gods, in the same way that Hephaestus and Arachne did.&quot; And you're going to have a market for those things, especially because a living god is currently in the process of conquering the world, and lots of people want to stop or support him. If you told someone in 2017 that you could make an invisibility cloak, they'd look at you funny and laugh about Harry Potter. If you told someone in 323 BCE, they'd say &quot;oh, word? I'm listening. Prove it.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T11:48:49-08:00","id":1045257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1045209#post1045209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Perfect, I like it, very cool! There's a Moros PC in my IRL game that's really into Anubis, so I've got some ideas for you. I might leave open exactly what the monster is, and we'll figure out exactly where you guys start geographically once more characters come in.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Baalim was just a note to self that the monster that I hunt could be a man. The character is still evolving but I am sure the basics are set. I wanted him to be the master of the soul so I was looking at the possibility of having atleast a passing knowledge of the arcanum associated with the five parts of the soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T11:55:22-08:00","id":1045264,"title":"","content":"There also isn't a sharp distinction between Mages and everyone else. The Weret-Hekau don't believe the Scorpion Dynasty (Nameless Empire from Mummy) was doing anything different in kind, just being more reckless about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T12:06:05-08:00","id":1045274,"title":"","content":"Well, yeah, I get that we're not going to think of ourselves as primitive Mages or think of ourselves as being historical figures. That would be weird.<br /> <br /> I did get the book and I'm looking through it, and man oh man... well, whatever. I'm not gonna gripe about CofD vs nWoD, though I am super salty they threw out the Atlantean myth. Good job OPP.<br /> <br /> ANYWAY!<br /> <br /> So that's gonna be my character concept. An Obrimos Arcadian Gnostikon. And his shadowname is definitely going to be &quot;Cyclops&quot; because of the following. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poseidonius_(mechanician\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poseidonius_(mechanician</a>) is going to have been his mentor, and Polyphemus, a cyclops was the son of Poseidon. Given his inclination for forging, that will be his thing. I imagine him also studying at the Pythagorean school, so he's definitely gonna be a smarty-pants character.<br /> <br /> Any restrictions you're planning on imposing? And for the rest of the players, do we want to pool some of our merit dots together for a Sanctum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder","name":"Silver_Smoulder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12852_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T12:06:55-08:00","id":1045275,"title":"","content":"Ya I was reading about that, I find it all fascinating. I am captivated by the Ancient Egyptian and Aztec culturs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T12:10:32-08:00","id":1045280,"title":"","content":"Since we already have an Obrimos I guess my Persian Magi is going to be an Acanthus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 02-07-2017, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T13:07:18-08:00","id":1045327,"title":"","content":"We can have overlap, no? I plan on focusing on Prime and Matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder","name":"Silver_Smoulder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12852_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T13:13:05-08:00","id":1045330,"title":"","content":"I don't think that overlap hurts and if Exthalion wishes to also run a Obrimos that should work. I think that we need the four cultures covered and if we have 5 players that on overlap but the paths shouldn't matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T13:21:33-08:00","id":1045337,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> Here is a picture I like for him","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 02-08-2017, 04:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T14:14:10-08:00","id":1045377,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1144_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1144\" data-vbnamecard=\"1144\">Exthalion</a> Yeah, that's actually something I want to run with. Mages in this era don't put things into separate boxes as much as moderns do, they're more about similar effects than different causes. If you meet a vampire, it's going to be less &quot;a Nosferatu of the Ordo Dracul with 3 dots in Theban Sorcery&quot; and more &quot;this guy is a sorcerer too, but his unenlightened technique requires <i>way</i> more blood sacrifice than yours.&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> There's an Aztec chapter in Dark Eras called Beneath The Skin, it's wild. I'd love to run/play in that setting.<br /> <br /> Overlap between Paths and Archai is alright with me, but you guys can resolve that how you want. You don't need every Arche represented. Warning: the PCs in my IRL game have lots of Fate but no Matter, and I constantly throw Matter Mysteries at them just to mess with them. I would prefer all of the Great Cults be represented, and at least 3 Darshanas. My personal faves are the Mantra Sadikhi and the Samashti, so pick those if you want to curry my favor.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12852_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12852\" data-vbnamecard=\"12852\">Silver_Smoulder</a> Didn't mean to pick on ya, you just gave me an opening to say stuff about the setting that I left out of the previous post. If you're interested in exploring Atlantean ruins, they're still there and we can definitely do that in this game! I'm one of those people who was really turned off by the focus on Atlantis in 1E Mage, at least the way most books depicted it, but I know setting changes like that can be a downer.<br /> <br /> Cyclops was always my favorite mutant. Nice historical find, maybe Poseidonius can be the group mentor. Or you can certainly have more than one NPC mage in your life, maybe you were introduced to the other one through him. We'll see how it shakes out.<br /> <br /> I'm still cooking up the rules side of things, but maybe don't buy Hallow? You'll have to find those yourself. Sanctum/Safe Place is okay, but those Merit dots are going to represent having set up a secure ritual space when you move to a new location, rather than one constant fortress. Think those Bioware games where your party members hang out at the spaceport in each &quot;world.&quot; Buy Social merits with the understanding that you're going to be moving around a lot, although I'll be working with you, not punishing you for buying Allies. Otherwise no restrictions I can think of. Feel free to buy Artifacts and stuff, those are way more interesting than Ambidextrous and Iron Stamina. If you get a Familiar, we'll work together on stats but you can definitely draft them yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T14:29:25-08:00","id":1045391,"title":"","content":"Can we buy magic items from other splats like mummy relics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T14:38:20-08:00","id":1045399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1045391#post1045391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we buy magic items from other splats like mummy relics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have something specific in mind? If it's in a book, I'll look it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T14:47:24-08:00","id":1045405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1045399#post1045399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you have something specific in mind? If it's in a book, I'll look it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not right now. I know that Magi can use written texts as magic tools and one of the categories of mummy relics is texts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T14:48:39-08:00","id":1045406,"title":"","content":"I would like a travelling companion of a Sleepwalker, but I am relatively new to Mage: the Awakening and not sure how to get a Sleepwalker. Is he a retainer with the sleepwalker merit, is he an ally? how many merit/experience is he?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T15:29:34-08:00","id":1045430,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1144_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1144\" data-vbnamecard=\"1144\">Exthalion</a> I'm open to it but I'd want to work with you on the specifics. I need to dust off my Mummy books, but I've run it before and basically know the rules. I would probably have it count as a Path tool in the way that Artifacts do along with its actual power. If you see one you like, let me know.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> That's totally fine! I was thinking someone might do that. Retainers don't have full stats like a PC does, they just roll a dicepool based on the number of dots in the Retainer merit. (This is how I run most NPCs, too.) But to give you access to the Sleepwalker merits, let's do this.<br /> <br /> <b>Sleepwalker Retainer (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Retainer or True Friend<br /> Your retainer or true friend is a Sleepwalker. They can remember magic and hold spells for you. Dots in this Merit give them the benefits of the following other Merits, found on Mage 305-306.<br /> \u2022: Banner-Bearer 1<br /> \u2022\u2022: Ritual Savvy OR Ritual Martyr<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022: Banner-Bearer 2<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: Deadpan OR Loved OR Relic Attuned<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: Banner-Bearer 3<br /> <br /> Also, for everybody, here's the difference between Retainer and True Friend in my games. True Friend gives 1 Willpower once per chapter for a meaningful interaction, not once per story. They usually roll dice as a 3-dot Retainer, but to make up for their extra benefits, they have more ability to do their own thing and potentially say no if you ask for help. There's always a risk that a Retainer can potentially be subverted, killed, or turned against you (although my goal is to make the game interesting, not screw you over), but a True Friend doesn't have those risks unless you ask for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T16:23:41-08:00","id":1045460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silver_Smoulder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1045274#post1045274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that's gonna be my character concept. An Obrimos Arcadian Gnostikon. And his shadowname is definitely going to be &quot;Cyclops&quot; because of the following. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poseidonius_(mechanician\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poseidonius_(mechanician</a>) is going to have been his mentor, and Polyphemus, a cyclops was the son of Poseidon. Given his inclination for forging, that will be his thing. I imagine him also studying at the Pythagorean school, so he's definitely gonna be a smarty-pants character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just throwing this out there, but have you considered a Moros Forgemaster? They have matter and the legacy gives Prime.<br /> <br /> Not trying to talk you out of Obrimos, might go Acathus myself regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 02-07-2017, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T18:57:25-08:00","id":1045561,"title":"","content":"Okay, well, right now I'm still trying to get a &quot;feel&quot; for my guy, so not sure yet. Moros Forgemaster could work, but I imagine that Stygia and Greeks don't mix really well. But maybe! I'll have to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder","name":"Silver_Smoulder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12852_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T01:47:24-08:00","id":1045655,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://i855.photobucket.com/albums/ab116/cdjensen99/Setau2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Setau \u2013 The Hand of Anpu (Warrior Priest of Anpu)<br /> <b>Shadow Name:</b> Strife<br /> <b>Path:</b> Moros<br /> <b>Darshanas:</b> Vajrastra<br /> <b>Great Cult:</b> Weret-Hekau<br /> <b>Legacy:</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037811-2e-stone-scribes-legacy-update#post1037811\">Stone Scribes</a><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Conceptually I would like the soul to be the focus of his Occult studies, knowing the Five Parts of the Soul.<br /> <br /> Skills divided between fighting, knowledge. He will need Craft, Weaponry, Athletics, Intimidation, Occult. Probably Medicine and investigation also.<br /> Merits he will need True friend, and Sleepwalker Retainer (As described above)<br /> Arcana he will have Death, Fate, and Matter. (More if point permit)<br /> Attributes Primary is Physical, Secondary is Mental Tertiary is Social.<br /> <br /> The Five Parts of the Soul (Correspond to)<br /> <b>Ren:</b> Fate (the name)<br /> <b>Ba:</b> Mind (Identity and passion)<br /> <b>Sheut:</b> Death (Shadow Aspects)<br /> <b>Ka:</b> Prime (vital essence)<br /> <b>Ab:</b> Spirit (Heart of the Soul)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Companions:</b> Sleepwalker True Friend (Wife) &amp; Jackal.<br /> <br /> <b>Awakening Event:</b> While travelling between Memphis and Abydos he was attacked by some bandits and left for dead. He had a waking dream of standing in light to have his soul weighed when Anpu pulled him from the line. Told that he was to have a greater fate and was charged with the sacred duty of collecting the names of the dead. Upon awakening he was whole again and felt strong. He journeyed back to Memphis as an Awakened sought out and joined the Stone Scribes, became a warrior priest.<br /> <br /> <b>Conceptual Background:</b> <br /> Setau was an architect by trade prior to the Awakening, viewed that Awakening as a sign from the God and became a Warrior Priest. Father was the Tax collector in Memphis.<br /> <br /> Left Egypt to track a great beast that decimated a small village outside of Memphis. Tracking the Beast to Babylon where he lost track of it. Near to Alexanders Court he sought assistance in tracking the beast in unfamiliar territory. This would introduce him to his mentor and a group of other wandering mages. He befriended his soon to be mentor as he pledged his service.<br /> <br /> On one knee \u201cBy the Might of the all-powerful Anpu, I pledge my service\u201d and thus his journey began.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000ff\">Conceptually I feel I am done, I can fill out the sheet when I know more about he Character creation guidelines, no rush. Can fill out more about the other and how we met when i know more about them.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 02-08-2017, 08:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T04:04:59-08:00","id":1045675,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> this may interest you: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_golden_wolf#Taxonomic_history\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Africa...onomic_history</a><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T04:34:40-08:00","id":1045683,"title":"","content":"Thanks that was an interesting article.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:30:03-08:00","id":1045775,"title":"","content":"<b>Everybody who's interested: </b>Post your Path, Cult/Darshana, and exactly five sentences answering the question &quot;What's your character's deal?&quot;<br /> That's all the backstory I need or want right now. (Hardwire, you're all set for now, thanks for getting Strife up.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:51:36-08:00","id":1045792,"title":"","content":"Shadowname: Antikatoprismos<br /> Pelasgian Gnostikos on the path of Moros<br /> <br /> A student of the Pythagorean school, Antikatoprismos was an apprentice underneath the great Siege Master and Mechanician Poseidonis. He reached Supernal truth relatively late, when he was 30 and has participated in several of Alexander's conquests, giving him both a knowledge of war, war machines, war logistics, and so on. Taking on the name &quot;Cyclops,&quot; after an injury he suffered early on in life, and to represent his skill with machines, he now seeks to create Platonic mechanisms, ones that would surpass any current device, and to perhaps even surpass his master.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder","name":"Silver_Smoulder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12852_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T09:51:48-08:00","id":1045826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1045775#post1045775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Everybody who's interested: </b>Post your Path, Cult/Darshana, and exactly five sentences answering the question &amp;quot;What's your character's deal?&amp;quot;<br /> That's all the backstory I need or want right now. (Hardwire, you're all set for now, thanks for getting Strife up.)</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Is there still room to join?<br /> <br /> 2) Do I need Dark Eras to play? (the whole thing or just the section pertaining to Mage?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T09:57:11-08:00","id":1045832,"title":"","content":"There shold be room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T10:01:16-08:00","id":1045836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1045826#post1045826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) Is there still room to join?<br /> <br /> 2) Do I need Dark Eras to play? (the whole thing or just the section pertaining to Mage?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah feel free to post a character. You don't need Dark Eras, I'm posting the stuff you need as a player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T11:49:02-08:00","id":1045890,"title":"","content":"<b>Name:</b> Hepsu<br /> <b>Shadow Name:</b> Smsw wAt Jj m htp (Follower on Imhotep's way) (Imhotep for short)<br /> <b>Path:</b> Sheut (Moros)<br /> <b>Cult:</b> Weret-Hekau<br /> <b>Darshana:</b> Seba (Jnanashakti)<br /> <br /> Hepsu was a scribe in Abydos. He was educated in a broad amount of topics, like law, medicine and alchemy. After inhaling fumes from his reagents, he had a near-death experience. During his Awakening and early apprentienceship he was followed by Urbi, a wolf spirit, which was given a body by his then-teacher. He seeks to form his making broadly, involving embalming, alchemy, medicine, wards and postcognition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T12:50:23-08:00","id":1045920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1045836#post1045836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah feel free to post a character. You don't need Dark Eras, I'm posting the stuff you need as a player.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nevermind, lol. I know next to nothing of this era or cultures and the amount of research I am having to do to get educated and form a coherent character is overtaking my studies (just tryin to choose a Hindu name and research gods). <br /> <br /> I was going to make a Thyrsus Samashti/Mantra Sadikhi that followed Vishnu and delves deeply into extreme body transformation/mutilation to obtain the vessel most adequate for receiving Vishnu's next avatar. The perfect form most likely resulting in a nightmarish abomination of ascetic order that indiscriminately enforces some self-proclaimed doctrine of order.<br /> <br /> Funny enough, I think I would have faired better with Aztecs, but it is better if I try to find a game set in modern times as I find it more intriguing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks anyway!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T13:04:21-08:00","id":1045928,"title":"","content":"Fair enough! Thanks for checking in, and you made the right call putting school first and not tumbling down the research wormhole.<br /> <br /> FYI for anyone else on the fence: I'm really trying to avoid that &quot;hours reading about ancient animal husbandry on wikipedia&quot; phenomenon for this game, both for myself and you potential players. If you're interested but don't have a full character idea or don't know the setting that well, just post what you're thinking so far (&quot;i wanna be a spirit tamer/disillusioned soldier/trickster witch&quot;) and we can talk out ideas together. I'm not a historian and I'm gonna be making up lots of stuff for this game, don't be afraid to just dive in and make statements about your character and the world. It's a historical setting, but the only audience is you guys, we're not being graded or anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T13:08:58-08:00","id":1045933,"title":"","content":"I just picked up this setting the other day and I would be glad to help anyone that wants it. Really I don't have much of a life outside of work so I would be glad to help others if needed.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2207\" data-vbnamecard=\"2207\">Caladriu</a> That also goes for you if you need anything just let me know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 02-08-2017, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T13:17:02-08:00","id":1045942,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> I was just thinking that the area of this setting I know the least about is Persia, the Achaemenids, Zoroastrians, what the Karpani are all about. Do you think you could do a little writeup of interesting stuff for using the Persian chunk of this game? Not like a wikipedia page, just interesting stories and characters and places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T13:21:14-08:00","id":1045947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1045942#post1045942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> I was just thinking that the area of this setting I know the least about is Persia, the Achaemenids, Zoroastrians, what the Karpani are all about. Do you think you could do a little writeup of interesting stuff for using the Persian chunk of this game? Not like a wikipedia page, just interesting stories and characters and places.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I will see what I can whip up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T14:46:54-08:00","id":1046011,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s a bunch of short character sketches that anyone can use as a starting point.<br /> <br /> <b>Jnanashakti</b><ul><li><b>Arcadian:</b> Philosophical \u201cdetective\u201d who uses reason and Socratic questioning (think Umberto Eco) to solve murders and enigmas.</li> <li><b>Karpani:</b> Calligrapher who practices the magic of the written word, searching for secret languages and forbidden texts.</li> <li><b>Mantra Sadhaki:</b> Carefree poet seeking the stories, songs and fables of other supernatural beings.</li> <li><b>Weret-Hekau:</b> Master of water and rivers, especially the Nile, studying magical properties of foreign, Shadow, even Underworld rivers.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Mahanizrayani</b><ul><li><b>Arcadian:</b> Admirer of Aristotle\u2019s <i>Poetics </i>who summons the Muses to help exalt and guide Sleepers through theatre and drama.</li> <li><b>Karpani:</b> Freelance judge and Prime expert who reveals those who deceive others, and empowers those who stand for truth.</li> <li><b>Mantra Sadhaki:</b> Ascetic who aims to inspire mages by generating Pneuma/anything else they need solely within their own body/mind/soul.</li> <li><b>Weret-Hekau:</b> Spirit/Death/Mind unifier seeking to find commonalities between the ephemeral worlds and syncretisms between foreign gods.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Samashti</b><ul><li><b>Arcadian:</b> Soothsayer inspired by Alceste/Admeto who tests people by imposing character-building hardships or granting gifts they can\u2019t possibly repay.</li> <li><b>Karpani:</b> Quiet refugee trying to derive meaning from trauma of war, and lead Sleepers to escape the cycle of suffering that imprisons the Mind.</li> <li><b>Mantra Sadhaki: </b>Thread-Cutter assassin who judges the worth of souls, cutting short beggars and emperors whose time has passed.</li> <li><b>Weret-Hekau:</b> Devotee of Set and eternal outsider, slaying the monsters who live in the wastes and chaotic places so people can sleep safe and ignorant.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Vajrastra</b><ul><li><b>Arcadian:</b> Macedonian soldier who was with Alexander\u2019s army from the beginning, now worried that the emperor has been corrupted by sorcery.</li> <li><b>Karpani:</b> Warrior at Gaugamela, perverse admirer of Alexander\u2019s brutal conquest, trying to draw magic from slaying powerful individuals like he did.</li> <li><b>Mantra Sadhaki</b>: Practitioner of body-mastering yoga, would-be greatest archer in the world.</li> <li><b>Weret-Hekau:</b> Aristocratic Nubian swordsman claiming magical weapons in the name of the people who truly deserve to wield them.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Acanthos:</b> Wanderer tossed by a chaotic world who hasn't seen home in many years. Fearful oracle haunted by a monster within the loom of the Fates that lurks in their own undefined future. Disciplined soldier who takes oaths, promises, and contracts extremely seriously.<br /> <br /> <b>Mastigos:</b> Gambler and game-player who uses games of chance and skill to practice a secret talent for strategy and warfare. Cartographer for Alexander's armies who deserted with a map to heaven. Introspective summoner who conjures their own dreams to serve them.<br /> <br /> <b>Moros: </b>Soldier-necromancer who binds ghosts into each piece of their armor. Exorcist who resolves spectral hauntings and psychological trauma. Obsessive Orphean searching for their lost love in the Underworlds of different lands.<br /> <br /> <b>Obrimos:</b> Eccentric birdwatcher seeking to become lighter than air and teach humans how to fly. Counterspell expert who dispels magic that does not serve the cause of truth and justice. Warrior mage who swore an oath to only use tools and weapons conjured with Prime from the realm of forms.<br /> <br /> <b>Thyrsos:</b> Wilderness ascetic who reluctantly re-entered human society, but still prefers the company of animals. Hippocratic healer who uses Life to advance Sleeper medical knowledge. Trickster spiritualist taking advantage of the Alexander-induced chaos in the Shadow for personal gain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 02-08-2017, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T23:45:58-08:00","id":1046200,"title":"","content":"<b>Name:</b> Shahpur<br /> <b>Shadow Name:</b> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khvarenah\" target=\"_blank\">Khvarenah</a><br /> <b>Path:</b> Acanthos<br /> <b>Cult:</b> Karpani<br /> <b>Darshana:</b> Mahanizrayani - Dasturs<br /> <br /> Shahpur was once a respected astronomer, trained in Babylon no less, who was forced to sell his services as an astrologer and fortune teller to survive after he fled before the conquering Iskandar. Obsessed with his failure, he watched each night as the stars grew brighter until their silver rays had grown long and sharp, and the whole of the sky was a hedge of thorns. Transfixed by fate stronger than steel he realized that Zarathustra had been right all along; the world is a prison for evil and we are caught in it. Yet when he remembered Iskandar, meaning to curse him one last time, the way forward and to freedom suddenly became clear. Fate is not a cage except to those who fear it; to the free, the thorns are knives to cut the world into new shape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 02-09-2017, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T02:11:22-08:00","id":1046220,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#0000ff\">Not sure how detailed you want me to get with this but here is some of the stuff I have been able to glean. Are you wanting a summery of what is in the book for those that do not have the book or are you wanting a real world accurate view of it all? I personally know nothing of the area but can research anything you want.</span><br /> <br /> In the game the Karpani went into hiding until things settled down. BTW Has Alexander died in the game yet? Because that would shape the Persian world, After his death they reclaimed the Iranian Valley.<br /> <br /> This is a real-world overview of the Persians. (Thought I would stop until I found out what you wanted so I wasn't researching the wrong thing)<br /> The Achaemenid Empire, also called the (First) Persian Empire, started in the Iranian Plateau and was founded by Cyrus the Great. The empire spread to be the largest of its time and at its height covered 2,123,562 sq mi and had a population of 17 \u2013 35 million people. Zoroastrianism (<i>Mazdayasna)</i> was the religion of the time and the Karpani were the priests.<br /> <br /> The Zoroastrianism holy text is the Avesta and in these texts <i>Zartosht</i> (Zoroaster is the Greek pronunciation) proclaimed that there is only one true God and he is Ahura Mazda (Ahura The Lord Creator, and Mazda, Supremely Wise). There are Spirits called Spenta Mainyu (literally translates to Immortals).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 02-09-2017, 05:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T11:41:08-08:00","id":1046392,"title":"","content":"That's not quite correct. The Karpani were soothsayers and hedge mystics, the priests were the actual Magi. Karpani represented pre-Zartosht Persian spirituality, and in fact were denounced by him as charlatans.<br /> <br /> After Alexander's death Persia was ruled by Hellenic Seleukides for quite some time.<br /> <br /> Of some interest is the fact dogs and golden jackals (!) were considered holy animals. <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Other (in)famous feature was the practice of Xwedodah.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T11:48:30-08:00","id":1046398,"title":"","content":"Ok as I said I am not familiar with the area or the history of the area. So I can only judge by what I read and that is only as accurate as the author was. But if you would like to be the fact checker/provider then that would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:37:43-08:00","id":1046424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1046220#post1046220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0000ff\">Not sure how detailed you want me to get with this but here is some of the stuff I have been able to glean. Are you wanting a summery of what is in the book for those that do not have the book or are you wanting a real world accurate view of it all? I personally know nothing of the area but can research anything you want.</span><br /> <br /> In the game the Karpani went into hiding until things settled down. BTW Has Alexander died in the game yet? Because that would shape the Persian world, After his death they reclaimed the Iranian Valley.<br /> <br /> This is a real-world overview of the Persians. (Thought I would stop until I found out what you wanted so I wasn't researching the wrong thing)<br /> The Achaemenid Empire, also called the (First) Persian Empire, started in the Iranian Plateau and was founded by Cyrus the Great. The empire spread to be the largest of its time and at its height covered 2,123,562 sq mi and had a population of 17 \u2013 35 million people. Zoroastrianism (<i>Mazdayasna)</i> was the religion of the time and the Karpani were the priests.<br /> <br /> The Zoroastrianism holy text is the Avesta and in these texts <i>Zartosht</i> (Zoroaster is the Greek pronunciation) proclaimed that there is only one true God and he is Ahura Mazda (Ahura The Lord Creator, and Mazda, Supremely Wise). There are Spirits called Spenta Mainyu (literally translates to Immortals).</div> </div> </div> </div>There were multiple sects of Zorastrianism, some of which were closer to dualism, holding that Ahura Mazda and Angra Mainyu were equal in power.<br /> <br /> Spenta Mainyu is actually one of the Amesha Spenta (lit. Immortal Bounteous) There were six and are the prime emanations (or whatever the appropriate term is) of Ahura Mazda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:57:37-08:00","id":1046434,"title":"","content":"Okay, y'all are clearly comfortable with Persia, which is great. I might tap you for ideas when we're there.<br /> <br /> Here's stuff to think about<b></b>:<br /> Your shared mentor is a woman of the Mantra Sadhaki. Tell me her Path, her Darshana, her Legacy, and a magical Merit or unusual ability/trait she has. Also tell me one interesting thing your PC did or learned from her. She travels, but each of you has spent a few weeks in her company somewhere in the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:06:33-08:00","id":1046443,"title":"","content":"Hey, if you by chance still accept people into your game, then I'd love to be one of them. So, here is my character's basic concept, let me know if something is not to your liking.<br /> <br /> Name: Alketas<br /> Shadow Name: Chor\u00eds periorismo\u00fas (&quot;the Unbound&quot;)<br /> Path: Mastigos<br /> Great Cult: Arcadian Mysteries<br /> Darshana: Phulakeion<br /> <br /> Alketas is a young Macedonian farmer-turned-officer who fought alongside Alexander's army from the first day. Fascinated by his sheer force of will and the ability to shape the world like clay, he sought to master himself, body and mind. He Awakened while on a scouting mission back in Egypt, captured by a mad willworker. As his captor's blood dripped from his sword and he explored his new abilities as well as the mage's writings, he begun to understand one thing: the world is a test, and if you pass - Awakening and then complete self-control is your reward. However, there are those out there who failed and want you to fail, their foul magic like cancer that needs to be cut out - so that's what Alketas does, hunting stray mages and otherworldly entities so that humanity may have a chance at taking its rightful place as masters of the universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10396,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","user":"Woland","date":". 02-09-2017, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:32:05-08:00","id":1046458,"title":"","content":"Thumbs up, you're in. I'll have some character questions for all the PCs later today. Feel free to tell us something about the shared mentor and where you encountered them!<br /> <br /> FYI, we're gonna start in Upper Egypt with the mentor having asked you to find something out in the desert. I've been statting up an adventure that should be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:48:19-08:00","id":1046465,"title":"","content":"<b>Path:</b> Moros<br /> <b>Darshana:</b> Jnanashakti<br /> <b>Legacy:</b> Uncrowned Kings<br /> <b>Merit:</b> Masque<br /> <br /> On his journey to hunt the beast He happened along a elder lady struggling with her load. He put her load within his cart and helped her into the seat. Along the way into Babylon she tested him, she was mean to see if he would become angry, she wept to see if he would lend an shoulder and a friendly ear, She interfered with the hunt to test his patience. Summoned beasts to test his courage, put herself in harms way to test his valor. She said that he was charming. On her last day with him she gifted him a Pendent (Imbued Item) that has the ability to charm snakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:59:48-08:00","id":1046469,"title":"","content":"Cool- other people can make suggestions too, if y'all have other ideas. I'm crowdsourcing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T15:52:34-08:00","id":1046508,"title":"","content":"Although the old woman mystified Alketas ever since they left Greece, his first meaningful encounter with her was a week after his Awakening, when he was assigned guard duty to her tent. At first, he was outraged, even more so when she abused her standing as (apparent) nobility to make him run meaningless errands for more than a month. During that time, from bits of conversation and observing her surroundings he surmised that she, too, possesses the gift of magic. So he confronted her about it, and the argument carried long into the night, becoming a philosophical dispute. That was when she offered to make him her apprentice, and he accepted, hoping she will provide him resources and opportunity to flourish. Besides, at the time he was convinced that not only is this woman a master alchemist and willworker, she also appears to have an influence on the court and more than a few spies in her service. Not a pleasant perspective to have her as an enemy.<br /> <br /> He's met the others some time later (perhaps on some previous assignment?).The woman gave her name as Alkmene, although Alketas is certain that's not her real or even shadow name. She has a clear sense of superiority, but apparently is quite loyal to fellow mages in her own, cliquish way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T16:31:49-08:00","id":1046518,"title":"","content":"It would actually be pretty convenient for her to be an Uncrowned King, one of the cabal's NPC pals in my home game is one of them and I've already converted the Legacy to 2E. I also just realized we have 3 Moros, wow. Gotta get my Death/Matter stuff ready.<br /> <br /> <b>Strife, </b>you were an architect, right? Have you ever studied a structure that had magical properties, and what were they? Your wife must be very patient to travel with you in your magical work, what's she like? Is this beast physical or spiritual, and what do you know about it?<br /> <br /> <b>Antikatoprismos, </b>is Poseidonius a magician like you? What is one magical thing you've seen while with the army? How did you leave Alexander's army? What is one magical item you would like to create? What's a name with fewer syllables we can call you?<br /> <br /> <b>Imhotep, </b>have you ever visited the tombs in Abydos from the Scorpion Empire? How do you feel about the Weret-Hekau who try to keep them from being plundered for magic in the present? What's Urbi like? Who is a non-Awakened supernatural being that you know in Abydos?<br /> <br /> <b>Khvarenah, </b>who is someone you're sorry to have lost contact with when Iskandar invaded? What is the worst fortune you ever told? What is a magical Mystery related to the stars that you wish to pursue? How do the more folksy Karpani feel about your educated urban background, and you about theirs?<br /> <br /> <b>Unbound, </b>did the wicked sorcerer who captured you have friends? What did you see with the army that still stays with you? When did you come closest to death while fighting an otherworldly monster? Do you venerate any of the gods or heroes in particular? Have you ever encountered the Tyrannoi, a philosophical school whose adherents also seek to master the universe?<br /> <br /> <b>Strife and Imhotep,</b> you're both Weret-Hekau aligned to Sheut. Does that make you friends, or rivals? How are you different, apart from hailing from Memphis and Abydos respectively? Did you meet while studying with your mentor, or elsewhere?<br /> <br /> <b>Antikatoprismos and Unbound,</b> did you encounter each other in Alexander's army on the trail? Did you leave together, or reconnect later? What do you think the emperor's next move will be?<br /> <br /> <b>Khvarenah,</b> where did you meet these yahoos exactly? Who is your mentor's other student from Persia, and why aren't they traveling with you now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 02-09-2017, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T17:08:17-08:00","id":1046531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1046434#post1046434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, y'all are clearly comfortable with Persia, which is great. I might tap you for ideas when we're there.<br /> <br /> Here's stuff to think about<b></b>:<br /> Your shared mentor is a woman of the Mantra Sadhaki. Tell me her Path, her Darshana, her Legacy, and a magical Merit or unusual ability/trait she has. Also tell me one interesting thing your PC did or learned from her. She travels, but each of you has spent a few weeks in her company somewhere in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some thoughts:<br /> Mantra is a sacred utterance with spiritual power<br /> Sadhaki means one who is following a particular spiritual path but has not reached their goal<br /> Taken together the shadow name seems to imply one who is on a spiritual path that makes use of certain spoken phrases or sounds.<br /> <br /> <b>Legacy:</b> Cryptologos (Or rather an ancient High Speech focused equivalent)<br /> <b>Darshana: </b>Jnanashakti<br /> <b>Path:</b> Mastigo, Sets us tests and trials just a little beyond our ability in order to allow us to break past our limits and scour away our preconceptions and self-delusions<br /> <b>Merit:</b> Grimoire: She is the latest in a line of disciplic succession that orally passes down a holy, magic-laden, scripture. &quot;Ordaining&quot; a successor involves passing it to them or creating a copy at which point the recipient can remember it perfectly.<br /> <br /> Besides teaching Khvarenah the High Speech, his mentor also helped him make peace with his god.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1046518#post1046518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Khvarenah, </b>who is someone you're sorry to have lost contact with when Iskandar invaded?</div> </div> </div> </div>Shahpur had a friend in the palace guard, Adarbad. They knew each other since they were boys, and it was Adarbad's good natured persistent misunderstanding that led to Shahpur learning how to do astrology and fortune telling at all. He left with Darius and Shahpur has not heard from or of him since.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1046518#post1046518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the worst fortune you ever told?</div> </div> </div> </div>A man asked how he could ensure his sons grew to be righteous men. Khvarenah answered, &quot;You must sin, so they may know how not to.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1046518#post1046518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is a magical Mystery related to the stars that you wish to pursue?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are marks of ancient magic upon the stars. Empty voids where their light was swallowed, broken constellations where fate was wretched into a new course, and stranger things besides. Yet between these wounds, Khverenah has glimpsed the shape of something else, older still and vaster. He would know what was done to break the sky and what was thereby hidden.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1046518#post1046518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the more folksy Karpani feel about your educated urban background, and you about theirs?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's complicated... He views his education and greater exposure to different people and ideas an advantage in many situations but does not believe that they make him intrinsically better or automatically superior in every respect to the rest of the Karpani.<br /> <br /> For their part, they fall into two camps. The first thinks he looks down on them and that his statements to the contrary are presumption to make him look better. The other feel like they are drowning under the need to fill the role of spiritual teacher and look to him like a lifeline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1046518#post1046518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Khvarenah,</b> where did you meet these yahoos exactly? Who is your mentor's other student from Persia, and why aren't they traveling with you now?</div> </div> </div> </div>His mentor introduced him to the Weret-Hakau because he needed safe passage into Khemet for his astrological studies. The Hellens were part of her efforts to help him move past his resentment to Iskander and those like him.<br /> Out of Character, I don't know how many or if there are other students from Persia. I got the impression most mages don't have more than one apprentice at a time, so the lot of us could be a little overwhelming even if we were all trained in sequence.<br /> <br /> Most other Persian mages are more interested in Persia. Some want to throw out the Hellens, some are focused on protecting Persian culture or assiting the people. Few are galavanting about looking for messages left by Ahura Mazda in the stars.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 02-10-2017, 02:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T02:00:48-08:00","id":1046686,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:blue\">You were an architect, right?</span></b> Correct<br /> <b><span style=\"color:blue\">Have you ever studied a structure that had magical properties, and what were they?</span> </b>Not a whole building but I would say that he would have studied a Burial Chamber in a pyramid &amp; a Sarcophagus that was magical. The Pyramid being from the Sixth Dynasty the Tomb of Mentuhotep II.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:blue\">Your wife must be very patient to travel with you in your magical work, what\u2019s she like?</span> </b>She is his Sleepwalker and true Friend so yes she is very patient. She is respectful of her place as his wife and his duties to the Lord Anpu. Marrying into his family was a step up for her and her family. She is strong willed, almost as strong as he is, and will not tolerate abuse. But other than that she feels that it is her duty to take care of her husband in all of his duties/endeavors.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:blue\">Is this beast physical or spiritual, and what do you know about it?</span> </b>I do not know if this makes sense but I look at the beast as his ID/Super Ego taken manifest, it was created from a karmic event that is his counter balance in the Fallen. He can chase it forever and will never catch it. It is one of his Obsessions, his eternal Mystery.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:blue\">You're both Weret-Hekau aligned to Sheut. Does that make you friends, or rivals?</span></b> Until the forming of the cadre we are probably acquaintances. Having traveled to Abydos a handful of times and not staying for any length of time, they know each other.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:blue\">How are you different, apart from hailing from Memphis and Abydos respectively?</span></b> He is a scribe the scholarly type I am a Warrior Priest. I cannot attest to his outlook on life but it is probably more to the Supernal where I look at magic as a weapon from Anpu to serve his need in the fallen. His only non-warrior task from Anpu is to collect the names of the dead (Stone Scribe)<br /> <b><span style=\"color:blue\">Did you meet while studying with your mentor, or elsewhere?</span></b> Abydos is more likely where we met.<br /> <br /> Expanded view of the Beast<br /> I view the beast as an extention of me. When he became Awakened paradox leaked into the world, took shadow flesh form, the coalesced into the beast. The beast could be human mage, Supernal/ephemeral entity, or what ever you want, but it is Abyssal in nature. We are linked together I can't destroy him nor can he destroy me. His actions spur my actions that guide his original action, kind of like a Fate/time loop. Just my thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 02-10-2017, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T05:03:14-08:00","id":1046718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1046518#post1046518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also just realized we have 3 Moros, wow. Gotta get my Death/Matter stuff ready.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you need I can change to an Acanthus or Obrimos. Most everything would stay the same. I have been wanting to play an Acanthus Mage. When we first started to talk about the game I stated an Acanthus or an Obrimos but other stated that was what they were looking at so I changed to Moros.<br /> <br /> It would be a fast change so let me know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 02-10-2017, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T11:13:18-08:00","id":1046847,"title":"","content":"<b>Did the wicked sorcerer who captured you have friends? </b><br /> The sorcerer didn't have many friends, but his family is a wealthy and old clan of Apophis-worshipping Proximi merchants, especially active in Upper Egypt.<br /> Infernalism (well, an equivalent of it, anyway) and debauchery in pure form and they aren't exactly fond of some Greek barbarian killing their own. Alketas doesn't realize<br /> most of this, although the deceased had a family crest (or something close to it) on him, so he knows that there is some group of people after him important enough to have a symbol. <br /> <br /> <b>What did you see with the army that still stays with you? </b><br /> Once, in Damascus, he watched a carpenter club to death three of the elite Greek infantry that looted his house and killed his family, only to be then hacked to pieces by <br /> their friends. He took that as a lesson that strenght is nothing when guided by rage, and it is better to strike at your foes when you have a tactical advantage, or<br /> better yet - manipulate the situation so that it resolves itself.<br /> <br /> <b>When did you come closest to death while fighting an otherworldly monster? </b><br /> He had many close calls, but he was mere inches from death not two months ago, when he was about to catch an old, leprous Banisher in the deserts of Persia.<br /> Far too late did he realize that the mage was wearing him down and leading him into a trap. He woke up a day later in a goatherder's hut, almost dead and not necessarily<br /> victorious (he doesn't remember much from the confrontation and isn't even sure what part of those memories were made up by his delirious mind). He nearly perished because of<br /> the mage's worst sin - hubris.<br /> <br /> <b>Do you venerate any of the gods or heroes in particular? </b><br /> He is not a devout worshipper, but if anything he pays respects to Athena, in her aspect focused on power, enlightenment and warfare as means to an end, rather than the goal<br /> itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Have you ever encountered the Tyrannoi, a philosophical school whose adherents also seek to master the universe?</b><br /> Alketas once &quot;found&quot; a brief and hardly complete (or entirely accurate) research on the Tyrannoi subject in his mentor's tent, but he never met one personally.<br /> Although he wouldn't shy away from working with one, it is his belief that it is wasteful to use magic for the sole purpose of gaining temporal power and wealth, rather than<br /> perfecting one's inner self and pushing others to do so. <br /> <br /> As for the &quot;joint questions&quot; for me and Antikatoprismos I think that the odds of us meeting in the army before Awakening are pretty low, given that I was mostly on the front lines, while he was tending to machines. However, we could leave (or at least hang out) together, figuring that our talents and magic compliment nicely. Or we could be introduced by the mentor we (the team) have. As for Alexander's next move - Alketas figures he will push further east, to northern India and probably stay there for a while. The word &quot;enough&quot; is absent from the Emperor's dictionary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T13:00:23-08:00","id":1046891,"title":"","content":"I am fine with changing over to Obrimos. It might be interesting if I could craft my own legacy similar to that of the Moros crafters.<br /> <br /> <u>Is Poseidonius a magician like you? </u><br /> Nope, entirely mundane. But Antikatoprismos wants to surpass him without drawing on the Supernal... or alternatively, Awaken the old man.<br /> <br /> <u>What is one magical thing you've seen while with the army?</u><br /> Antikatoprismos hasn't seen it himself, but his buddy told him of a shadow, a <i>vrykolak</i> who stalked towards two sentries, took them out without a noise, and then began lapping at their blood. Fire spooked it away, which is why his friend survived.<br /> <br /> <u>How did you leave Alexander's army?</u><br /> At &lt;insert battle here&gt; a blow from an enemy mace as he was defending the siege engines ended up knocking one of his eyes out. That left him to just build and maintain the siege engines and not fire them, so he left of his own volition, but promised to be &quot;on call&quot; if another conquest is to occur.<br /> <br /> <u>What is one magical item you would like to create?</u><br /> Like the legends of the Cyclops, he wishes to forge thunderbolts, to rain lightning on the enemy from up in the clouds, to rival the power of Olympus itself! Hubris? Never heard of it.<br /> <br /> <u>What's a name with fewer syllables we can call you?</u><br /> Prism would work, especially if I change to Obrimos.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Antikatoprismos and Unbound,</b> did you encounter each other in Alexander's army on the trail?</u><br /> I would be cool with that.<br /> <br /> <u>Did you leave together, or reconnect later?</u><br /> I definitely had my character leave before his Awakening, so presumably at different times, but because I'm still on-retainer for the Army, we can still keep in touch.<br /> <br /> <u>What do you think the emperor's next move will be?</u><br /> Presumably once he finishes politicking, march further, to spread Civilization even further. There's lands to the North and East, after all...<br /> <br /> <br /> Your shared mentor is a woman of the Mantra Sadhaki. Tell me her Path, her Darshana, her Legacy, and a magical Merit or unusual ability/trait she has. Also tell me one interesting thing your PC did or learned from her. She travels, but each of you has spent a few weeks in her company somewhere in the world.<br /> <br /> At the point when he was working out on his Theorem of Supernal Geomtries, he encountered her as a willworker in Alexandria. She and him had several debates over the course of a month over whether machines imitate life or life imitates machines. He had her pegged as a Thyrsus based on her arguments or maybe an Acanthus. In any case, she never parted with a piece of broken compass, that she claimed would help her find the way back to the Watchtowers again.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder","name":"Silver_Smoulder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12852_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T13:48:21-08:00","id":1046910,"title":"","content":"Good stuff. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6508_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6508\" data-vbnamecard=\"6508\">Tambov</a> once you weigh in, I'll make an OOC thread and give some character creation rules, and we can probably start playing this weekend.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12852_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12852\" data-vbnamecard=\"12852\">Silver_Smoulder</a> I'll leave it up to you guys, but if you wanted to switch to Acanthus or Obrimos respectively, that would be good. It sounds like Prism is more about Matter than Matter+Death anyway, and Obrimos would make magic item stuff easier. I'm down with you creating a new Legacy in game, that's a great excuse for an Obsession about studying Awakened crafters from different traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T14:01:28-08:00","id":1046921,"title":"","content":"I will give her fist shot at Obrimos, else I will switch to Obrimos. Then we will have an Acanthos, Mastigos, 2 Moros, and an Obrimos. I haven't given much thought to playing a Thyrsos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T14:27:14-08:00","id":1046926,"title":"","content":"Coolbeans! So it sounds like this is shaping up rather nicely. I'm pretty excited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder","name":"Silver_Smoulder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12852_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T01:10:19-08:00","id":1047116,"title":"","content":"<b>Path:</b> Moros or Thyrsos<br /> <b>Darshana:</b> Jnanashakti<br /> <b>Legacy:</b> Uncrowned Kings<br /> <b>Merit:</b> Grimoire<br /> <br /> Would like to have met her after taking a wrong turn and getting lost in the Necropolis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1046518#post1046518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Imhotep, </b>have you ever visited the tombs in Abydos from the Scorpion Empire? How do you feel about the Weret-Hekau who try to keep them from being plundered for magic in the present? What's Urbi like? Who is a non-Awakened supernatural being that you know in Abydos?</div> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>Abydos: I've been there, placing funeral offering for the long dead as a gesture of respect (and Oblation).</li> <li>Guardians: doing gods' work paying respect to our ancestors (Urbi thinks it a waste of Artefacts, but has enough Finesse to be subtle about it)</li> <li>Urbi: affectionate, but savagely protective when pushed. Possessive, likes to hog attention. Plays the role of an effigy of Anapa during cultural Oblations. Has a conditionally indefinite body made for her for as long as the Familiar bond persists, would like to keep it as long as possible.</li> <li>Other supernaturals: Tut-ankh-hathor, a vampire attending nightly offerings at the mausoleum of Sethi I</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1039592-looking-for-a-pbp-mage-game?p=1046518#post1046518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Strife and Imhotep,</b> you're both Weret-Hekau aligned to Sheut. Does that make you friends, or rivals? How are you different, apart from hailing from Memphis and Abydos respectively? Did you meet while studying with your mentor, or elsewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>Friends or rivals: friends, probably</li> <li>Differences: I see Magic through the lense of Science and Occult, rather than Athletics and Weaponry.</li> <li>Meeting: we probably met when he came to Abydos on some official buiseness.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T09:17:11-08:00","id":1047260,"title":"","content":"Ch-check it out: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1047257-ooc-awakening-2e-to-the-strongest\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/g...-the-strongest</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}